Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||12-13-2001||07:18 AM||||Hey I'm sure you will be back on the road in no time.<BR>I lost everything in a house fire 3 years ago, it has taken a long time but we have replaced most of the things we lost.<BR>On a positive note I probably would not own a Fiero it it hadn't been for that fire.<BR>Lost my 74 camaro to the blaze.<P>Keep up the good work.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">                   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CHSpiff_1.gif">                   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">                    <BR>                        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jake_Dragon (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||12-13-2001||07:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>Wow, thats all I can say.  Is it justmainly body damage?  Did any of the wiring in the dash get melted?  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yeah I have lost a lot of wiring. Is worse than it looks when you start to look really closely. Brakeline finally blew today which made me almost drive it through my new garage door. Suprisingly it does still run even though the main loom under the dash is a blob of melted plastic.<P>||||reg||1
